  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.4.1 (forks 2.4.1) - WebGPU, WebGL and Wasm drop the debug assertions before code generation, so the dead index/length compare chains of every ArrayView access are no longer emitted (TRELLIS.2 GEMM WGSL 592 KB -> 331 KB, cold first launch 6.6 s -> 1.25 s), and WebGPU loads each scalar slot once at kernel entry (fixes a DXC E_FAIL phi of resource handles; attention -11 %). See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.0 (forks 2.4.0) - Velocity, the SIMD CPU backend, is a complete backend and the default CPU backend: AllAccelerators() / AllAcceleratorsAsync() register it instead of the plain CPU accelerator on desktop and server (BEHAVIOR CHANGE: the plain CPU accelerator is the debugging backend now, register it with builder.DefaultCPU(); 32-bit processes keep it, the browser registers no CPU accelerator). Velocity runs all 731 shared tests: Half, BFloat16, FP8, FP4 and packed 4-bit types, 1D/2D/3D grids and groups, groups of up to 256 threads with fast barriers, Vector256 / Vector512 device types. MathF.Truncate / Math.Truncate work on every compiled backend. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.3.9 (forks 2.3.14) - FIXED: a loop with a compile-time trip count inside an if, whose result is used after the if, returned the value from before the loop in every thread that took the branch, on CUDA, OpenCL, WebGPU, WebGL and Wasm (LoopUnrolling left the exit block phi naming the cleared loop header as its source). See CHANGELOG.md.",
